; damped least-squares inverse of the Jacobian
; solves: delta-theta = J^T (J J^T + lambda I)^{-1} * error
; minimum-norm solution for the underdetermined system J * delta-theta = error
; lambda (seema) damps the inverse near singularities, preventing blow-up
; iterative: krama of Newton-Raphson steps converges to the IK solution
; sangati roots: viparita (inversion), seema (lambda = damping threshold),
; krama (iterative steps), viveka (choosing minimum norm)

(kosha dls-pseudoinverse
  (swarupa tinanta bhave-prayoga viparita)
  (sthita domain-robotics)
  (siddha krama viveka ik)
  (yukta seema norm-seema)
  (nirodha singularity)
  (viparita jacobian)
  (phala minimum-norm joint-space))
